summary:
  The rail's answer is scrolled to while the footer still has the height it had before the rows.

history:
  The answer's rows go into the model in the callback, and a Column lays
  them out only at the next frame. Measured on a real ListView: without the
  forced layout a thirty-row answer put the view at 1424 with its heading at
  1600, under the fold of a 200-pixel view, exactly the screen the rails
  showed before the reveal existed.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ViewLogic.js

find:
      if (typeof f.forceLayout === "function") f.forceLayout();

replace:
      if (false) f.forceLayout();

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_viewlogic.qml::test_a_long_answer_shows_its_heading_at_the_top.
  Line-neutral.
